== Teaching and writing ==

Ralston's Cheng Hsin work combines martial arts instruction with bodywork, facilitation, and studies of consciousness. His own interviews and organization-affiliated publications describe his approach as emphasizing direct experience, physical awareness, and effective interaction rather than fixed technique.<ref name="tqj">{{cite interview
 |last=Ralston
 |first=Peter
 |title=Interview with Peter Ralston
 |work=Tai Chi Chuan Journal
 |publisher=tqj.de
 |url=https://tqj.de/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/tqj-online-Interview-Ralston-407.pdf
 |access-date=September 25, 2026
}}</ref><ref name="taijivizier">{{cite interview
 |last=Ralston
 |first=Peter
 |title=Tai-Chi interview with Peter Ralston
 |work=Taijivizier
 |publisher=Stichting Taijiquan Nederland
 |url=https://www.chenghsin.nl/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/Tai-Chi-Interview-met-Peter-Ralston.pdf
 |access-date=September 25, 2026
}}</ref>

